{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power","id":898948,"title":"Lunar Charms - shapeshifting, or monstrous power?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-25T08:29:09-07:00","id":898948,"title":"Lunar Charms - shapeshifting, or monstrous power?","content":"Twin-Faced Hero seems like a proper Lunar Charm, to me. Luna's Chosen can emulate their goddess by blurring the line of &quot;man or woman&quot; as easily as she and they can blur the line of &quot;man and beast&quot;... or even &quot;me and him&quot;.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Shaping the Ideal Form (the original First Edition Lunar Charm which included the male/female effect) seems Lunar to me. Since Lunar Exalted are to be identified across forms through their Tell, it doesn't matter as much if their true human face remains the same from day to day -- anyone who sees their basic form will see their Tell, and anyone who sees their Tell will recognize their basic form later, just as they could spot and recognize the Tell in any of their stolen forms.<br /> <br /> <br /> But outside of <i>that one Charm</i>, I don't feel that shapeshifting actually works for Lunar Charms so much as the aesthetic of &quot;raw power, uncontrolled and psychotic&quot;. Bestial power. Not the power of animals, but the power that makes people think of wild beasts. Power that makes beasts of men.<br /> <br /> (Please note that Lunar Charms are entirely different from Heart's Blood shapeshifting, which very much does grant Lunars the powers of animals, by letting them assume the <i>forms</i> of those animals. But a Lunar using a Strength Charm in a lion form isn't adding the strength of the lion to the strength of the lion. He is adding the unfettered, monstrous strength of the Mad Moon Goddess to the form of the lion. He is becoming the monstrous Nemean Lion of myth and legend; a beast sent by the gods to carry out their wrath on Earth.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Consider this: A Lunar equivalent to Solar Strength-Increasing Exercise will probably make the Lunar twice as large from the swelling of his muscles and bones. But growing twice as massive could be explained as his body swelling to contain the divine, bestial strength now surging through his body, rather than his body shapeshifting into a stronger form. The growth becomes the side-effect rather than the method. The method becomes tapping into elemental strength. Psychotic, unrestrained strength.<br /> <br /> If a Liminal Exalt were to do something similar, adding more muscle and bone would certainly be the method rather than the side-effect, because the Liminals are the Exalted of the raw materials of the physical body. They're not strong because of divine, bestial power, but because they use dark magic to steal from the corpses of others to reinforce their frankenstein bodies.<br /> <br /> <br /> Consider this: An Intelligence equivalent to the Lunar Charm above wouldn't cause the Lunar's head to swell to twice its size to contain his mad brilliance. That sort of grotesque and ridiculous image inspires disgust rather than awe, and thus doesn't fit the divine, celestial nature of Lunar power. It is the sort of thing that Liminal Exalted do, because their entire aesthetic is about being repulsively wet and meaty and bulging in all the wrong places.<br /> <br /> Instead, the Lunar Charm might express the strain upon the Lunar by imposing a derangement. The Lunar's mind expands, his inner eyes opening up to the truths of the universe, but this short-cut to enlightenment drives him temporarily mad. To maintain his sanity, he might obsess over a singular goal, bending his mad genius to that pursuit until the task is done or the magic wears off and leaves him sane again. This would be far more fitting of Lunar imagery.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monkey Arm Technique isn't Lunar. It's a Liminal Exalt horrendously stretching and tearing their flesh and bones to reach farther than should be physical possible, likely making them spray blood everywhere. It's weird and gross and messy.<br /> <br /> Armor-Forming Technique isn't Lunar. It's a Liminal Exalt pushing their bones to the outside in order to form a disgusting exoskeleton for protection.<br /> <br /> Weapon-Trapping Body Dominion is a Liminal congealing their blood and wrapping their meat and bones around a sword to disarm someone who stabbed their frankenstein body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:56:56-07:00","id":898972,"title":"","content":"Snake-Head Defense, though.<br /> But also, re:Monkey-Arm Technique, it doesn't need to be an exclusive thing either. Using a different example: Abyssals get blood-chain appendages, lunars (might) get tentacle ones, liminals might get zombie limbs. These are not necessarily completely exclusive things. Just because one can find different and more personally-appealing fluff for it doesn't mean the splat should lose it entirely. Though I agree that Weapon-Trapping Body Dominion is really out there for Lunars and Monkey Arm Technique feels more like a holdover from 1e which helped dilute Lunars in 2e. It has &quot;body mastery&quot; themes, like Dhalsim, but doesn't really fit with the skinwalker vibe of lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:17:25-07:00","id":898995,"title":"","content":"Canon-wise, I suspect that all the themes you're highlighting will be downplayed in Lunars' (eventual) 3E portrayal. There's been a lot of talk about focusing them on animal myth-aspects, rather than &quot;shoggoth stuff&quot;.<br /> <br /> But since I've always wanted Lunars to be less werewolf and more Hindu myth, I'm all ears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:18:04-07:00","id":898996,"title":"","content":"I think <i>primal</i> power might be a better way to describe the main principle in discussion - as to include things such as drawing upon ancient knowledge from blood and bone or the earth itself, and manifestations of spiritual and shamanic acuity - but I agree with the proposed thesis for the most part. Fata-Ku makes a sensible point that there can be a little mechanical overlap in some things for those splats without falling out of their themes or impeaching on each other's shticks.<br /> <br /> I don't expect tentacle-appendage-ing though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-25-2016, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:24:48-07:00","id":899000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=898996#post898996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't expect tentacle-appendage-ing though.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no real reason that they shouldn't have tentacle Charms, just so long as they're animal tentacles, like on a squid, and not shoggoth tentacles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-25-2016, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:59:54-07:00","id":899053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=899000#post899000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no real reason that they shouldn't have tentacle Charms, just so long as they're animal tentacles, like on a squid, and not shoggoth tentacles.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true. The issue isn't so much individual charms, as it is, how all these charms come together.<br /> Should a Lunar be able to sprout wings. Since they can emulate various animals, I would say yes.<br /> Should a Lunar be able to have multiple heads? Now, I've always seen them not as animals per-se, but as mythical representations of animals. They're not 'a lion', they're 'the king of beasts'. And since things like Hydra's are a great source of inspiration, I would say so.<br /> Should they be able have tentacles, definatly.<br /> Can they regrow entire limbs like lizards? Surely they can.<br /> <br /> If you have all of these at the same time, you're a flying, regenerating mass of snakeheads and tentacles, which starts becoming quite shoggothy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T10:11:33-07:00","id":899067,"title":"","content":"I feel like if you get there by that route you've kind of earned it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T10:17:56-07:00","id":899073,"title":"","content":"I think they can have the monster themes foremost, and then there are Charms that literally change the body (whether it be shining claws or shooting snakes from wounds) in service to that as needed on a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> There have been comments in the past to the effect of &quot;divinity would have greater prominence than literal physical enhancements&quot; with regards to whether or not a Lunar would need to increase muscle size to increase strength.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of the Lunar theme could be conveyed through synergies between Charms rather than just characteristics for individual Charms. Including some things that go for a more overt divine image; shooting blades of moonlight ala the Burn Legend Okami overdrive, made distinctly Lunar by the circumstances in which it can be used and not being tied to a specific fighting Ability.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T10:38:48-07:00","id":899112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=898972#post898972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snake-Head Defense, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love the concept. I've repeatedly asked for it. I still want it, though I want it mechanically expressed as an environmental hazard centered around your body, with the specific form of the hazard depending on tastes. Snake hair, shadow-rats swarming up out of your shadow and vanishing just as quickly, BEES, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> I'm also going to work on a &quot;grow wings&quot; Strength Charm. Preferably one that takes into account how awkward wings ought to be on bodies that shouldn't have wings. Maybe growing wings on a form with Legendary Size ought to require a separate Charm purchase in itself (that is, aside from Towering Beast Shape making Legendary Size forms accessible in the first place).<br /> <br /> And as I said, I don't want to abandon &quot;Shaping the Ideal Form&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I'd like things like &quot;raw strength&quot; and &quot;raw intelligence&quot; to arise from raw, primal power, rather than from &quot;I shapeshift myself to have more Attribute dots, lol&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T11:58:39-07:00","id":899227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=899000#post899000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no real reason that they shouldn't have tentacle Charms, just so long as they're animal tentacles, like on a squid, and not shoggoth tentacles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's sensible for them to have tentacles in some manner, but I don't expect to see quite as many Charms focused on particular animal transformations in the likes of the aforementioned 1e tentacle chain. Not just because of the vague comments Isator brought up, but because it strikes me as more... decentralized and bizarre aesthetically than the devs would maybe for Lunars in 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-25-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:03:13-07:00","id":899230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=899000#post899000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no real reason that they shouldn't have tentacle Charms, just so long as they're animal tentacles, like on a squid, and not shoggoth tentacles.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's probably a non-spirit, <i>Dragon Quest</i> Slime-esque creature in Creation <i>somewhere</i>.<br /> <br /> If Lunars can grow wings, they can grow extra arms (like the spider-woman in the comic), and they can grow tentacles.<br /> <br /> They might even be able to grow extra legs, to go all Sleipnir and Catbus and centaur-man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T12:53:44-07:00","id":899289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=898995#post898995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's been a lot of talk about focusing them on animal myth-aspects, rather than &quot;shoggoth stuff&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shoggoth stuff fits both &quot;shapeshifting&quot; and &quot;monstrous power&quot; beautifully, though. It just doesn't fit werewolf/animal themes, or silver Solar themes. Looking at this as a two-sided argument is probably misleading, it's messier than that.<br /> <br /> Here are the major conflicting views on Lunars as I see them...<br /> <br /> Like Solars, but with Attributes<br /> Werewolves/animal people<br /> Shapeshifters<br /> Mythical monsters in general<br /> Barbarians<br /> Tricksters and free spirits<br /> Protectors<br /> <br /> These overlap, obviously, but combining them all together will give you a pretty incoherent splat. Which might actually be the least bad option here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T13:48:53-07:00","id":899350,"title":"","content":"My response to this is, and this is all pretty YMMV... I see where you're coming from with the idea of &quot;Psychotic, unrestrained strength&quot; - Lunars and the moon are associated with madness and tapping into imagery of lunar werewolf transformation links to that idea of an inner bestial might being unleashed and transformation and shapeshifting as relatively secondary to this, and the association of the attributes links to the idea of a raw magic.<br /> <br /> The problem for me with this is I don't, fundamentally, associate Luna as a moon deity with unrestrained strength. She's not really the Incarna that is, if any of them are. Luna often feels more devilish crafty and flexible, ruling over the night by her cunning, than uncontrolled and mighty in native strength.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say she's in control exactly, more her thing is being changeable, unfixed, and that's where madness comes in to her, and the idea of being a monster inside (as that's linked to this idea of having hidden fundamental forms within yourself that are quite different from who you are on the surface).<br /> <br /> Kind of a notion, this is actually what she is as a deity of the moon. The Moon can be defined as the celestial object that changes its form, and is casts its light from the night sky. So I guess to me this is why Lunars embody shapeshifting, and that shapeshifting is associated with the retreat of the rational, daylight world for the obscurity of night, and with passing from the human state to the more irrational and intuitive animal state, and with ruling over the night.<br /> <br /> (Where by analogy, mythologically, as the sun rises and sets, the Solars represent the natural cycle of the zenith heights of brilliance and might and cyclic declines of power, to be reborn and resurgent again, and the Sidereals stand with the distant, fixed symbols of the heavens, hidden during the daylight hours that provide secret maps for human navigation (physical and spiritual) in which man can trust to light the way, if they are wise enough to bear witness.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:05:09-07:00","id":899372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=899350#post899350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My response to this is, and this is all pretty YMMV... I see where you're coming from with the idea of &quot;Psychotic, unrestrained strength&quot; - Lunars and the moon are associated with madness and tapping into imagery of lunar werewolf transformation links to that idea of an inner bestial might being unleashed and transformation and shapeshifting as relatively secondary to this, and the association of the attributes links to the idea of a raw magic.<br /> <br /> The problem for me with this is I don't, fundamentally, associate Luna as a moon deity with unrestrained strength. She's not really the Incarna that is, if any of them are. Luna often feels more devilish crafty and flexible, ruling over the night by her cunning, than uncontrolled and mighty in native strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unconquered Sun was once statted out as having a Manipulation rating in the toilet compared to the rest of the Incarnae. This never stopped the Solars from being the very best spies or politicians, and given that one of the Lunar Castes has a theme of being super-physical in every way, and Strength Charms are a thing, there's something to latch onto that involves very straightforward feats of might (which is one of the things for which Full Moons are famed).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't say she's in control exactly, more her thing is being changeable, unfixed, and that's where madness comes in to her, and the idea of being a monster inside (as that's linked to this idea of having hidden fundamental forms within yourself that are quite different from who you are on the surface).<br /> <br /> Kind of a notion, this is actually what she is as a deity of the moon. The Moon can be defined as the celestial object that changes its form, and is casts its light from the night sky. So I guess to me this is why Lunars embody shapeshifting, and that shapeshifting is associated with the retreat of the rational, daylight world for the obscurity of night, and with passing from the human state to the more irrational and intuitive animal state, and with ruling over the night.<br /> <br /> (Where by analogy, mythologically, as the sun rises and sets, the Solars represent the natural cycle of the zenith heights of brilliance and might and cyclic declines of power, to be reborn and resurgent again, and the Sidereals stand with the distant, fixed symbols of the heavens, hidden during the daylight hours that provide secret maps for human navigation (physical and spiritual) in which man can trust to light the way, if they are wise enough to bear witness.) </div> </div> </div>Okay, but the descriptions of her Chosen explicitly call them out as being akin to &quot;children of her greatest union&quot; with Gaia, and bestial as a result. There's no real reason to not have a &quot;Get Obviously Swole&quot; Charm, and in fact this concept dates back to the first edition STC, when it was called Mighty Thews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:14:05-07:00","id":899384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=899067#post899067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like if you get there by that route you've kind of earned it though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem becomes when becoming a chimerical ball of mismatched limbs and organs becomes the One True Build.<br /> <br /> If you can learn a Charm to grow wings, and armor, and multiple heads, and tentacles, and you can apply all of this to a Tyrant Lizard form to become Chthulu Rex, then shouldn't everyone?<br /> <br /> Martial Arts and Evocations still provide alternatives, but when you're forsaking those to fight with the forms of animals, part of the fun is being forced to keep changing in response to the changing situation.<br /> <br /> Sometimes you need to fly, and other times your flying form isn't as strong as your land-born form, so you land and change into the form that hits harder.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the ability to mix your spirit shape and become a chimera through your totem, but being so chimerical that your forms lose distinction is undesirable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then again, taking the heart's blood of a large, tough-scaled, flying dragon achieves nearly the same end result of &quot;every advantage in one form&quot;... and then you stack tentacles on it.<br /> <br /> Ideally, anything stated out for flying like a winged dragon would still be built far more fragile than a land-bound beast like an ox-dragon, rather than smashing through stone structures and cliffsides without a care like <i>RWBY</i>'s Giant Nevermore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:24:58-07:00","id":899398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=898995#post898995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canon-wise, I suspect that all the themes you're highlighting will be downplayed in Lunars' (eventual) 3E portrayal. There's been a lot of talk about focusing them on animal myth-aspects, rather than &quot;shoggoth stuff&quot;.<br /> <br /> But since I've always wanted Lunars to be less werewolf and more Hindu myth, I'm all ears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on both points. Also the new Lunar focus included (at least for a time) the term &quot;culture hero&quot;, IIRC. I was never quite clear on how that was meant to distinguish them from Solars (because many classic Solar inspirations fall under that heading as it is commonly used) but I got the impression it was meant to evoke a hero with a strong sense of place..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:40:32-07:00","id":899413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=899372#post899372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no real reason to not have a &quot;Get Obviously Swole&quot; Charm, and in fact this concept dates back to the first edition STC, when it was called Mighty Thews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure, I wouldn't say they shouldn't. I'm more saying that I don't really feel much like the Lunars or Luna have a central and uniting theme of &quot;the aesthetic of &quot;raw power, uncontrolled and psychotic&quot;&quot;, so that doesn't work for me. I wouldn't say Lunars shouldn't have powers that boost their might because Luna is a cunning, adaptable goddess of night more than one of uncontrolled raw mighty one, just that I see that she *is* a cunning, adaptable, shifting goddess of night to me, first and foremost (and I think if you are going to be looked for any central unifying *thing* for Lunars, that's where we start looking).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T15:45:10-07:00","id":899475,"title":"","content":"shapeshifting, or monstrous power?<br /> <br /> How about both?<br /> <br /> To use your example, a Lunar turning into a mass of hulking muscle because of a strength charm... Regardless of how you fluff it, that's Shapeshifting. &quot;Literally growing my muscles to be stronger&quot; and &quot;turning into a muscular brute so as to channel the raw primal strength locked within me&quot; are not, really that diferant. You're body is still changing as a result of Lunar Power, you're still getting stronger, you're still turning into a muscular brute... Functionally the same thing.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, there are some effects that should be in the Lunar Tree that can't be fluffed as raw primal power<br /> <br /> A Lunar should be able to partial shapeshift. If knacks are gone(they've implied such) then that has to be a charm. A lunar should be able to grow natural weapons or make their existing natural weapons better. That's a strength charm. Possible several, if you want to progress from &quot;grow claws/make claws better&quot; to &quot;you know have silver claws that now channel the raw power of Luna in her most predatory aspect.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, Armor forming technique<b> is </b>Lunar. How many mythical monsters have scales, or shells, or hides that can't be pierced by mortal weapons? Lunars are the &quot;Mythical Beast&quot; exalted this time around.Growing such defensive measures or granting them to one's animal forms is more or less a mandatory part of the Lunar Charm tree..<br /> <br /> I've said this before, but what I'm expecting the Lunar Charm tree to be is low level-Attributes are enhanced supernaturally, but it's purely through the Lunar's magic, so no pysical changes yet. Mid levl charms are things like your body changing to maximize the effect of the lunar magic or changed into better forms by the lunar magic-improved musclemass becuase of primal mosnter strength, or primal monster strength because of improved monster mass. Hugh Level Charms are the &quot;form of the God Beast&quot; things-you're not just growing claws or making your animal forms claws better, you're channeling the raw and primal power o f destruction into claws made of Luna's own silver. You're not merly a massive Hulk of Flesh, your body, weather it's man or beast, it a body worthy of Celestial God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T16:01:06-07:00","id":899497,"title":"","content":"There are only two things important to me personally in the portrayal of Lunars in 3E. 1)Permanent form acquisition is done via violent methods- it makes a statement about their monstrous/bestial nature that I consider more important than any other facet of the Lunar identity. Temporary form acquisition can be done through other methods, I am a-ok with that and Forms are restricted to animals, which leads me to 2) Animal themed charm power-set, but not necessarily &quot;nature/balance/order&quot;. More like &quot;Primal&quot; or &quot;Instinctual&quot; through the realm of attributes rather than taxonomic descriptors that are only vaguely animal themed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:30:41-07:00","id":900205,"title":"","content":"It sounds workable to have permanently acquired forms need some kind of violence, I guess.<br /> <br /> I think if you did go that route, I think you do have to get rid of the whole &quot;The tattoos prevent shapeshifting sorcery being used&quot; thing, because it's a bit ludicrous for a Terrestrial to go and buy Disguise of the New Face and be able to perfectly duplicate an appearance with only &quot;a fragment of hair or skin, a drop of blood&quot; (stronger first version of the spell) or &quot;the target standing immobile&quot; (weaker second rewrite of the spell) and Lunars to not be able to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:27:11-07:00","id":900250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=899384#post899384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem becomes when becoming a chimerical ball of mismatched limbs and organs becomes the One True Build.<br /> <br /> If you can learn a Charm to grow wings, and armor, and multiple heads, and tentacles, and you can apply all of this to a Tyrant Lizard form to become Chthulu Rex, then shouldn't everyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's hella-expensive and those motes are committed, leaving you very little to improve your abilities to hit and not get hit, and now you've fucked up in the same way as Wyzen from Asura's Wrath when he went Gongen Wyzen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:29:33-07:00","id":900301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=900250#post900250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it's hella-expensive and those motes are committed, leaving you very little to improve your abilities to hit and not get hit, and now you've fucked up in the same way as Wyzen from Asura's Wrath when he went Gongen Wyzen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a dragon is its own reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:46:47-07:00","id":900320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/898948-lunar-charms-shapeshifting-or-monstrous-power?p=900301#post900301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a dragon is its own reward.</div> </div> </div> </div>But to reiterate, I hope that being a FLYING dragon carries real sacrifices compared to being a land-bound dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}